# Always Ask Questions on Solicitations

When ANY solicitation (RFP, ITB, RFI, RFQ, Sources Sought) offers a question submission period:

**ALWAYS draft and submit questions. No exceptions. No skipping.**

## Why

- Puts DDI's name in front of the Contracting Officer before the bid is even due
- Shows DDI did its homework and is a serious, qualified bidder
- Gets clarifications that strengthen the proposal
- Builds the relationship — COs remember who engaged early

## What to Do

1. When reviewing a new solicitation, immediately identify:
   - Questions deadline
   - Who questions go to (CO name/email)
   - Submission method (email, portal, BidNet, etc.)

2. Draft 3-5 smart questions that:
   - Show DDI read the full solicitation
   - Clarify scope, requirements, or evaluation criteria
   - Reference specific sections/pages of the RFP
   - Are NOT generic or obvious

3. Submit questions BEFORE the deadline — don't wait until the last day

4. Log in WORKFLOW_CHECKLIST.md:
   - Date questions submitted
   - CO confirmation (if received)
   - When answers are expected/posted

## What NOT to Ask

- Questions answered clearly in the solicitation
- "Can you extend the deadline?"
- Anything that makes DDI look like they didn't read the RFP
